==English==
[[Image:Tsetse_head-proboscis.jpeg|thumb|Head of a '''tsetse'''.]]

===Alternative forms===
* [[tzetze]], [[tsetze]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|tn|en}} {{term|tsetse|lang=tn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/tsitsi/|/sitsi/|/titsi/|lang=en}}
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/tsɛtsi/|/sɛtsi/|/tɛtsi/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|s|tsetse}}

# Any [[fly]] of the [[genus]] ''[[Glossina]]'', native to [[Africa]], that feeds on human and animal blood; known primarily as a carrier of parasitic [[trypanosome]]s.

====Usage notes====
* Particularly in North American English, this insect is most commonly referred to as a "tsetse fly."

